steps.body:
Questions give you a table of metal pairs and their voltages and ask you to interpret it. One idea explains almost every such table.

**The bigger the difference in reactivity between the two metals, the greater the voltage.**

So with a copper electrode fixed, and the reactivity series magnesium, zinc, iron, copper running from most to least reactive:

- **magnesium and copper** are furthest apart, so they give the **largest** voltage;
- **zinc and copper** give less;
- **iron and copper** give less still;
- **copper and copper** give **zero**, because there is no difference at all.

The **electrolyte** matters too. Change the solution and the voltage changes, which is why the specification lists both the electrode and the electrolyte as factors.

When you are asked to **interpret data**, do not just read off the biggest number. Say **why** it is biggest: because those two metals are furthest apart in reactivity.
